[{:db/id 17592186670576 :question/worked-solution "If $X\\sim\\operatorname{Po}(\\lambda)$, then its probability mass function is\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{\\lambda^x e^{-\\lambda}}{x!}.\n$$\n\nHere $\\lambda=1.1$, so\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{1.1^x e^{-1.1}}{x!}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(X=3)&=f(3)\\\\\n&=\\frac{1.1^3e^{-1.1}}{3!}\\\\\n&\\approx 0.0738419021.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRounded to four decimal places, the answer is $0.0738$." :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
